  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Green hydrogen valley &#x2013; Visit Indian delegation (CERF23IN1O)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">As part of the bilateral cooperation between India and the Netherlands on green hydrogen developments, CERF hosted a delegation of three government officials from the Ministry of New and Renewable Energy, Department Of Science &amp; Technology/CSIR and Ministry of Ports, Shipping and Waterways in India, during the World Hydrogen Summit &amp; Exhibition 2023 (WHS) in Rotterdam.The governmental delegation was combined with an Indian business delegation. Visiting WHS offered the delegation the opportunity to meet with other stakeholders in the sector, with a focus on setting up connections to government officials, business people and innovators from the Netherlands, in order to further explore cooperation.As part of the programme, CERF organised an one-day side visit to the hydrogen valley in the Northeast of the Netherlands, which was the first hydrogen valley appointed as such by the European Union (EU). In India, hydrogen valleys will also be developed and for the delegation it was of interest to see how in the Netherlands such regional green hydrogen economy is set up and what role public and private stakeholders have.The site visit included a visit to the RWE, Gasunie and Entrance, where a hydrogen testing facility was visited.</narrative>
  </description>
